 "result": "The mechanism is a tagging serializer. Each non-JSON type is wrapped in a single-key dict such as `{\" t\": [...]}`, and a marker class reverses it on load.\n\n- **`SignedCookieSessionInterface`** (`src/tessel/sessions.py:284`) is the default session interface. Its `serializer` attribute is `session_json_serializer = TypedCookieSerializer()` (`sessions.py:273`, `:300`). That serializer is passed to the signing serializer at `sessions.py:316`.\n- **`TypedCookieSerializer`** (`src/tessel/json/tag.py:219`) keeps an ordered registry of markers (`register`, line 256).\n  - `dumps` (line 321) calls `tag()` on each value before JSON-encoding.\n  - `loads` (line 325) JSON-decodes, then `untag()` rebuilds the original types.\n- **`TypeMarker`** (`tag.py:60`) is the base class for the markers. Each subclass implements the check, `to_json`, `to_python` and `tag()` for one type.\n  - `TagTuple` (line 133) stores a tuple as a list under a tag key.\n  - `TagBytes` (line 159) stores bytes as base64.\n  - `TagDateTime` (line 205) stores a datetime as an HTTP date string, using `http_date` and `parse_date`.\n  - `TagDict` (line 93) escapes user dicts that happen to look like tagged ones.\n  - `PassDict` (line 119) and `PassList` (line 147) pass plain dicts and lists through while still tagging their contents.\n  - `TagMarkup` (line 173) and `TagUUID` (line 191) cover `Markup` and `UUID`.",
